#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:6
msgid "Init hooks documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:10
msgid ""
"This document describes the init and power-state hook mechanism provided "
"by the `common/include/tlk_init.h` and `common/tlk_init.c` pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:12
msgid ""
"The system exposes several hook types that components can register. Hooks"
" are collected into dedicated linker sections by registration macros and "
"invoked by the runtime using the functions implemented in `tlk_init.c`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:14
msgid "**Primary goals:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:15
msgid ""
"Provide ordered initialization hooks (pre-init) for system, driver and "
"application code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:16
msgid "Provide lifecycle hooks for suspend/sleep transitions (before/after)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:17
msgid "Allow components to prevent suspend/sleep via boolean callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:19
msgid "Concepts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:21
msgid ""
"**Registration by linker sections:** Registration macros place function "
"pointers into named linker sections (for example, "
"`.pre_init_array_<level>_<priority>`). The build/linker is expected to "
"place these sections in an order that respects level and priority so the "
"runtime sees callbacks in the intended sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:22
msgid ""
"**Invocation:** Each public `tlk_*` function in `tlk_init.c` iterates "
"from a linker-provided `__*_start` to `__*_end` range and calls every "
"non-NULL function pointer it finds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:23
msgid ""
"**Ordering convention:** Lower numeric values indicate earlier/higher "
"priority. The headers define named level and priority constants (e.g. "
"`TLK_INIT_LEVEL_SYSTEM`/`TLK_INIT_PRIORITY_HIGH`). The final ordering "
"depends on the linker script that arranges the sections, but the numeric "
"convention should be used when registering callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:25
msgid "Levels & Priorities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:27
msgid "**Levels (examples):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:28
msgid "`TLK_INIT_LEVEL_SYSTEM` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:29
msgid "`TLK_INIT_LEVEL_DRIVER` = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:30
msgid "`TLK_INIT_LEVEL_APPLICATION` = 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:31
msgid "**Priorities (examples):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:32
msgid "`TLK_INIT_PRIORITY_HIGH` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:33
msgid "`TLK_INIT_PRIORITY_NORMAL` = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:34
msgid "`TLK_INIT_PRIORITY_LOW` = 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:36
msgid ""
"Use the level to group callbacks by broad stage "
"(system/driver/application) and use priority to fine-tune ordering inside"
" that stage. Smaller numbers mean higher precedence. Additional levels or"
" priorities are expected to be added in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:38
msgid "API reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:40
msgid "Initialization hooks (pre-init)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:42
msgid "**Type:** `typedef void (*tlk_pre_init_func_t)(void)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:43
msgid ""
"**Registration macro:** `TLK_REGISTER_PRE_INIT(fn, level, priority)` — "
"places the function pointer in `.pre_init_array_<level>_<priority>` and "
"marks it `used` so the linker doesn't discard it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developing/init_hooks.md:44
msgid ""
"**Invoker:** `void tlk_pre_init(void)` — iterates from `__pre_init_start`"
" to `__pre_init_end` and calls each registered function."
msgstr ""

